<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><title>Acceptable use — Cadastre</title><meta name="description" content="Responsible use of Cadastre's publicly browsable document research references."/></head><body><header class="site-header shell legal-header"><a href="/" class="wordmark">cadastre<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></a><a href="/#catalog" class="header-access">Browse the catalog ↗</a></header><main class="shell legal-page"><p class="eyebrow">PUBLIC RESEARCH</p><h1>Open references.<br/>Responsible use.</h1><p class="legal-version">Effective 26 October 2026</p><p>Cadastre's code, schemas, source index, and published reference images are publicly browsable. No application, DNS proof, organizational review, or access key is required to view them.</p><h2>Use the evidence responsibly</h2><p>Use these references for legitimate document research, identity verification, public service, education, or fraud prevention. Do not use them to create counterfeit documents, impersonate people or organizations, or bypass identity controls.</p><h2>Research limits</h2><p>Extracted images, normalized geometry, crop proposals, and source observations are research material. They do not independently establish document authenticity, complete coverage of a jurisdiction's designs, or calibrated physical measurements. Publications may contain annotations, illustrations, outdated designs, or incomplete specimens.</p><h2>Provenance and rights</h2><p>Follow the linked source publications and preserve attribution when using research findings. Public browsing does not transfer ownership of source materials or grant reproduction rights held by their publishers. Review the original publisher's terms for your intended use.</p><h2>Administrative access</h2><p>Publishing and administrative operations remain authenticated. Public browsing does not grant permission to modify the collection or access private operational records.</p><p><a href="/">← Return to Cadastre</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a></p></main></body></html>
